# AI Secretary — Clean Rewrite Walkthrough

## What Was Done

Deleted all old demo/mock Python files and **rewrote the entire codebase from scratch**, following the WAT framework from [CLAUDE.md](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/CLAUDE.md).

## New Project Structure

```
DA Project/
├── main.py                    ← Entry point
├── config.py                  ← Centralized .env config
├── orchestrator.py            ← WAT Layer 2: intent router
├── tools/
│   ├── outlook_client.py      ← Microsoft Graph API
│   ├── ai_engine.py           ← OpenAI with lazy init
│   ├── pdf_generator.py       ← HTML → PDF with pro styling
│   └── scheduler.py           ← APScheduler with callbacks
├── bot/
│   └── telegram_handler.py    ← Telegram bot
├── workflows/                 ← Markdown SOPs (kept)
├── CLAUDE.md                  ← WAT instructions (kept)
└── .env / requirements.txt
```

## Key Improvements Over Old Code

| Area | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| **Architecture** | Flat demo script | WAT layered (Config → Tools → Orchestrator → Bot) |
| **AI Engine** | Crashed on import without API key | Lazy init, keyword fallbacks |
| **Email Summary** | Flat text list | 🔴🟡🟢 urgency triage |
| **Email Drafting** | No approval flow | Draft → /approve → send |
| **PDF Slides** | Basic CSS | Professional slide theme |
| **Scheduler** | Jobs just logged | Real callbacks that execute + deliver via Telegram |
| **Telegram Bot** | Stub handlers | Full routing through orchestrator |

